From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: no boot hold for one large reservation or for V8's
 cage

Madeira reserved two ranges at boot for reservations a title had not made
yet: ml996 held the largest free hole for one large reservation of a size
madeira.cfg named (ml997 and ml1029 handed it out), and ml433 held
[0x7200000000, 0x7400000000) for V8's 8 GB cage. Both are gone, with the
calls that served from them: under decision 0183 no title sizes or
switches on an address-space hold, and a game's large reservations are
placed by the rules every game gets. A large ask that finds no room fails
as on any full address space.

Linear: PLA-843
Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/decisions/0183-no-per-game-memory-keys.md; tools/tests/test_elastic_reserve.py (host checks; phone gates not run)
Offered-upstream: no; the holds are the iOS port's
---
 build/ntdll-unix/loader_ios.c  |   9 -
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 305 +--------------------------------
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 312 deletions(-)

